findings.body:
The filter used to keep the URL only if it was a normal web page and not a reader-mode URL. It now keeps the URL if it is a web page or a reader-mode URL:

::diff{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/Toolbars/Redux/ToolbarMiddleware.swift" lines="482-486"}

`isReaderModeURL` checks for `http://localhost/reader-mode/page`, which is also an `http` URL, so `isWebPage()` is already true for it. With `||`, reader-mode URLs are always kept. When a user is in reader mode and taps Tabs, Menu or Cancel, the address bar gets `http://localhost:<port>/reader-mode/page?url=...` instead of a nil URL (which lets the toolbar fall back to its normal display).

Non-web URLs still map to nil, because `isReaderModeURL` is false for them, so the `||` only matters for reader-mode URLs.

::suggestion{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/Toolbars/Redux/ToolbarMiddleware.swift" lines="485-485"}
            url = (currentURL.isWebPage() && !currentURL.isReaderModeURL) ? url : nil

`gleanWrapper` changed from `private let` to `let`. Nothing outside the struct reads it; I grepped for `toolbarTelemetry.gleanWrapper` and found no hits. The other telemetry structs keep their wrapper private, so this only widens the API surface.

